            {
                "entry_id": "92a94139-2bf3-3bb9-9e52-8ec0aea689b2",
                "word": "nécrocratie",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "d85fa7ff-b121-41a6-84d4-bfee46eed52e",
                        "entry_id": "92a94139-2bf3-3bb9-9e52-8ec0aea689b2",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "nécrocraties"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "db397368-9367-3071-b5c1-3968f53aaa83",
                        "entry_id": "92a94139-2bf3-3bb9-9e52-8ec0aea689b2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Forme de gouvernement où une personne décédée est reconnue comme son chef ; généralement un ancien dirigeant décédé."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "d668b3db-08be-4ebf-bcec-595c84e25226",
                                "sense_id": "db397368-9367-3071-b5c1-3968f53aaa83",
                                "text": "Le calendrier commence à la naissance du premier Leader Suprême du pays, Kim Il-Sung (qui est toujours le big boss alors même qu’il est mort – c’est la seule nécrocratie du monde). Pff, baser un calendrier sur la naissance de quelqu’un, ridicule hein ?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "94e65b11-0b64-48c0-be95-f085a403019a",
                                "sense_id": "db397368-9367-3071-b5c1-3968f53aaa83",
                                "text": "Bravo, monsieur Bouteflika ! Vous avez excellé dans l’absurde. Vous avez battu Kafka et Beckett. Vous avez fait de l’Algérie une nécroratie, un étrange pays gouverné par un mort."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "8badfd10-9c1f-3954-ab64-104ae65157c5",
                        "entry_id": "92a94139-2bf3-3bb9-9e52-8ec0aea689b2",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Définition manquante ou à compléter. (Ajouter)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "577d9cb5-203f-483f-9cdd-b44fd10d79b5",
                                "sense_id": "8badfd10-9c1f-3954-ab64-104ae65157c5",
                                "text": "\"Poutine a capitalisé sur les penchants fatalistes de son pays pour en faire une nécrocratie, expliquant … qu’il valait mieux que les jeunes hommes meurent au combat que de la drogue ou de l’alcool, comme s’il n’y avait pas d’autre moyen de se réaliser : vivre une vie longue, paisible, heureuse et productive. Sous ce régime, il n’y a pas d’avenir, il n’y a qu’un passé à défendre\", déplore le philosophe Mikhaïl Epstein."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2e9a2c46-7288-4143-9bae-5a0acb3c7b25",
                        "source_entry_id": "92a94139-2bf3-3bb9-9e52-8ec0aea689b2",
                        "target_lang_word": "necrocracy",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "necrocracy",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "b6add695-99b1-30ba-9d99-30fc9b5ef751",
                                        "entry_id": "7a07092d-9502-3313-9fcd-225d6305a33d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A form of government imposed by those who have since died."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a35fdaf1-2380-490d-9aaa-9a1bbfca89e2",
                                                "sense_id": "b6add695-99b1-30ba-9d99-30fc9b5ef751",
                                                "text": "What we call democracy, therefore, is to a considerable extent necrocracy, or a form of government by the graveyards. Old precepts and phrases are handed down from one generation to another; they become part of a nation's heritage […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "30479aa3-0921-4182-9964-225c474e8d3f",
                                                "sense_id": "b6add695-99b1-30ba-9d99-30fc9b5ef751",
                                                "text": "Other activities became increasingly pressing, the Fellowship was flourishing and had plenty of younger members ready and able to take over from their elders; and I have seen too many cases of vigorous organisations gradually turning into gerontocracies and finally into necrocracies to wish ever to hold on to power myself."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "86827efd-0bde-4228-bb8d-194a64fe1aab",
                                                "sense_id": "b6add695-99b1-30ba-9d99-30fc9b5ef751",
                                                "text": "Further, even if one hundred per cent of the governed in 1789 fully supported the Constitution, the constitutional rule by the dead—one might call it necrocracy—is not democracy. Democracy requires self-government, which cannot be the dead ruling the living. Though legislators now dead passed many statutes now in force, a mere majority in the current Congress can repeal statutes but cannot amend the Constitution."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8dfaac62-26a6-4e63-9640-d0350218c6f7",
                                                "sense_id": "b6add695-99b1-30ba-9d99-30fc9b5ef751",
                                                "text": "Iran might still become a democracy, but it would also be a necrocracy: government of, by and for the dead."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "13f3984d-a17b-3a63-ad13-1e3efa326259",
                                        "entry_id": "7a07092d-9502-3313-9fcd-225d6305a33d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A form of government where a dead person is recognised as its head; usually a deceased former leader."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5d70d87f-2e5c-468c-891e-0ac3292e9b66",
                                                "sense_id": "13f3984d-a17b-3a63-ad13-1e3efa326259",
                                                "text": "Kim Jong Il, incidentally, has been made head of the party and of the army, but the office of the presidency is still \"eternally\" held by his adored and departed dad, who died on July 8, 1994, at 82. (The Kim is dead. Long live the Kim.) This makes North Korea the only state in the world with a dead president. What would be the right term for this? A necrocracy? A thanatocracy? A mortocracy? A mausolocracy?"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "238ae108-7503-4900-ad84-b02601681c1d",
                                                "sense_id": "13f3984d-a17b-3a63-ad13-1e3efa326259",
                                                "text": "The last king of Wanga Mukulu, Nabongo Rapando Lutomia, died in 1936; and the kingdom remained a necrocracy for seventy-three years until 2009 when his son, Prince Japheth William Wambani Rapando (1921–2012), was formally crowned nabongo."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bf5becee-53b7-4d04-bc6e-260f47b9c0fc",
                                                "sense_id": "13f3984d-a17b-3a63-ad13-1e3efa326259",
                                                "text": "The denomination of the 1985 Tito banknote was 5,000 dinars. It appeared in the era of advanced “necrocracy,” the rule of the dead President, at a time when the country's political leadership wanted to solidify his memory and associate themselves with “the greatest son of the Yugoslav peoples and nationalities.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "61cbb535-839b-3e43-8ba1-6b34c56ef716",
                                        "entry_id": "7a07092d-9502-3313-9fcd-225d6305a33d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A government ruled by the undead."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
